Rack-based coolant distribution units are essential components of liquid-cooling infrastructure, regulating and distributing coolant to maintain appropriate temperatures in high-density computing environments. They work with pumps, heat exchangers, reservoirs, and control systems to manage heat generated by servers and other electronic equipment.

The market is expanding as AI workloads and HPC applications generate increasing thermal loads that conventional air-cooling systems can struggle to manage efficiently. Rack-based CDUs enable more effective heat transfer and help data center operators support higher computing densities. North America currently leads the market due to its established data center infrastructure, while Asia-Pacific is emerging as a major growth region.

